WEBVTT


00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.600
Originally shown as a decorative
insertion, this classic eyelet

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.990
combination has lots of uses.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.110
Use it as a cast on edge, pick up
a neck line or an arm hole and work

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:17.850
it as a band, as an alternative to
ribbing or plain old stockinette.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:19.390
Her.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.690
We're using it as a bind off edge.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.850
Start with the carriage on the
left, pull the knitting out.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.080
Reach behind and work a
chain over the needles.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.850
Secure that last loop.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:05.069
Then free pass the carriage to pick
up the working yarn and knit one row.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.840
Transfer every other stitch
to its neighbor left to right.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:34.170
Pull the work out again, reach
behind and chain over those needles.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:52.800
Free pass to get the carriage
where the working yarn is.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.280
Knit one row.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:09.750
Transfer every other
stitch from right to left.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.570
It'd be the opposite of
the previous transfers.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:23.540
Knit a row.

00:02:30.915 --> 00:02:32.715
Chain one more time.

00:02:34.155 --> 00:02:36.705
You might find that working the
chain behind the knittings a

00:02:36.705 --> 00:02:39.165
little clumsy, but take your time.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.325
And the results are well worth it.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.680
And then bind off.

